---
import { Code } from 'astro:components'
import { docsTheme } from '../docs-theme'
import { docsHref } from '../site-links'
import { migrationComparison } from '../examples/migration-comparison'

const theme = docsTheme.expressiveCode.themes[0]
---

<section class="callout" aria-labelledby="xterm-heading">
  <div>
    <h2 id="xterm-heading">Coming from xterm.js</h2>
    <p>Fit, WebGL and Unicode graphemes are built in. Creation is async, and data stays as bytes from the PTY to the screen.</p>
    <p>Opening fits the host automatically. For an explicit resize, <code>grid</code> holds <code>columns</code> and <code>rows</code>; <code>send</code> is your PTY transport.</p>
    <p>Renderer options go in <code>opts</code>. <code>auto</code> selects WebGL2/WebGPU with canvas and DOM fallback. <code>gpu</code> is <code>WebGpuTerminalRenderer.create</code>; <code>dom</code> is <code>DomTerminalRenderer.create</code>.</p>
    <a href={docsHref('start/xterm')}>Read the migration guide</a>
  </div>
  <table class="map" aria-label="xterm.js to ghostty-webgpu">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">xterm.js</th><th scope="col">ghostty-webgpu</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{migrationComparison.map(({ from, to }) => (
      <tr>
        <td data-label="xterm.js"><Code code={from} lang={from.startsWith('@') ? 'text' : 'ts'} theme={theme} /></td>
        <td data-label="ghostty-webgpu">{to.map((code) => <Code code={code} lang="ts" theme={theme} />)}</td>
      </tr>
    ))}</tbody>
  </table>
</section>
